        "node_id": "n_3_d562d0",
        "thought_text": "The current approach using bitmasks to represent subsets of employees and their joke sets is inefficient for large N (up to 10,000) and doesn't correctly handle the constraints of the problem. Instead, we should use a dynamic programming approach that considers the tree structure of the company hierarchy and the constraints on joke sets. This approach will allow us to efficiently calculate the number of valid joke sets while respecting the rules about consecutive joke types and the hierarchy.",
